.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/postcss-import Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "postcss-import"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
.RS 4
\fRPostCSS\fP plugin to transform \fR@import\fP rules by inlining content\&. 
.RE
.PP

.PP
This plugin can consume local files, node modules or web_modules\&. To resolve path of an \fR@import\fP rule, it can look into root directory (by default \fRprocess\&.cwd()\fP), \fRweb_modules\fP, \fRnode_modules\fP or local modules\&. \fIWhen importing a module, it will look for \fRindex\&.css\fP or file referenced in \fRpackage\&.json\fP in the \fRstyle\fP or \fRmain\fP fields\&.\fP You can also provide manually multiples paths where to look at\&.

.PP
\fBNotes:\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBThis plugin should probably be used as the first plugin of your list\&. This way, other plugins will work on the AST as if there were only a single file to process, and will probably work as you can expect\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
This plugin works great with \fRpostcss-url\fP plugin, which will allow you to adjust assets \fRurl()\fP (or even inline them) after inlining imported files\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
In order to optimize output, \fBthis plugin will only import a file once\fP on a given scope (root, media query\&.\&.\&.)\&. Tests are made from the path & the content of imported files (using a hash table)\&. If this behavior is not what you want, look at \fRskipDuplicates\fP option
.IP "\(bu" 2
If you are looking for \fBGlob Imports\fP, you can use \fRpostcss-import-ext-glob\fP to extend postcss-import\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Imports which are not modified (by \fRoptions\&.filter\fP or because they are remote imports) are moved to the top of the output\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
**This plugin attempts to follow the CSS \fR@import\fP spec**; \fR@import\fP statements must precede all other statements (besides \fR@charset\fP)\&.
.PP
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-D postcss\-import
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Unless your stylesheet is in the same place where you run postcss (\fRprocess\&.cwd()\fP), you will need to use \fRfrom\fP option to make relative imports work\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
// dependencies
const fs = require("fs")
const postcss = require("postcss")
const atImport = require("postcss\-import")

// css to be processed
const css = fs\&.readFileSync("css/input\&.css", "utf8")

// process css
postcss()
  \&.use(atImport())
  \&.process(css, {
    // `from` option is needed here
    from: "css/input\&.css"
  })
  \&.then((result) => {
    const output = result\&.css

    console\&.log(output)
  })
.fi
.PP

.PP
\fRcss/input\&.css\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
/* can consume `node_modules`, `web_modules` or local modules */
@import "cssrecipes\-defaults"; /* == @import "\&.\&./node_modules/cssrecipes\-defaults/index\&.css"; */
@import "normalize\&.css"; /* == @import "\&.\&./node_modules/normalize\&.css/normalize\&.css"; */

@import "foo\&.css"; /* relative to css/ according to `from` option above */

@import "bar\&.css" (min\-width: 25em);

@import 'baz\&.css' layer(baz\-layer);

body {
  background: black;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
will give you:

.PP
.PP
.nf
/* \&.\&.\&. content of \&.\&./node_modules/cssrecipes\-defaults/index\&.css */
/* \&.\&.\&. content of \&.\&./node_modules/normalize\&.css/normalize\&.css */

/* \&.\&.\&. content of css/foo\&.css */

@media (min\-width: 25em) {
/* \&.\&.\&. content of css/bar\&.css */
}

@layer baz\-layer {
/* \&.\&.\&. content of css/baz\&.css */
}

body {
  background: black;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Checkout the [tests](test) for more examples\&.
.SS "Options"
.SS "\fRfilter\fP"
Type: \fRFunction\fP 
.br
 Default: \fR() => true\fP

.PP
Only transform imports for which the test function returns \fRtrue\fP\&. Imports for which the test function returns \fRfalse\fP will be left as is\&. The function gets the path to import as an argument and should return a boolean\&.
.SS "\fRroot\fP"
Type: \fRString\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRprocess\&.cwd()\fP or \fIdirname of \fRthe postcss \fRfrom\fP\fP\fP

.PP
Define the root where to resolve path (eg: place where \fRnode_modules\fP are)\&. Should not be used that much\&. 
.br
 _Note: nested \fR@import\fP will additionally benefit of the relative dirname of imported files\&._
.SS "\fRpath\fP"
Type: \fRString|Array\fP 
.br
 Default: \fR[]\fP

.PP
A string or an array of paths in where to look for files\&.
.SS "\fRplugins\fP"
Type: \fRArray\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRundefined\fP

.PP
An array of plugins to be applied on each imported files\&.
.SS "\fRresolve\fP"
Type: \fRFunction\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRnull\fP

.PP
You can provide a custom path resolver with this option\&. This function gets \fR(id, basedir, importOptions)\fP arguments and should return a path, an array of paths or a promise resolving to the path(s)\&. If you do not return an absolute path, your path will be resolved to an absolute path using the default resolver\&. You can use \fRresolve\fP for this\&.
.SS "\fRload\fP"
Type: \fRFunction\fP 
.br
 Default: null

.PP
You can overwrite the default loading way by setting this option\&. This function gets \fR(filename, importOptions)\fP arguments and returns content or promised content\&.
.SS "\fRskipDuplicates\fP"
Type: \fRBoolean\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
By default, similar files (based on the same content) are being skipped\&. It's to optimize output and skip similar files like \fRnormalize\&.css\fP for example\&. If this behavior is not what you want, just set this option to \fRfalse\fP to disable it\&.
.SS "\fRaddModulesDirectories\fP"
Type: \fRArray\fP 
.br
 Default: \fR[]\fP

.PP
An array of folder names to add to \fRNode's resolver\fP\&. Values will be appended to the default resolve directories: \fR["node_modules", "web_modules"]\fP\&.

.PP
This option is only for adding additional directories to default resolver\&. If you provide your own resolver via the \fRresolve\fP configuration option above, then this value will be ignored\&.
.SS "\fRnameLayer\fP"
Type: \fRFunction\fP Default: \fRnull\fP

.PP
You can provide a custom naming function for anonymous layers (\fR@import 'baz\&.css' layer;\fP)\&. This function gets \fR(index, rootFilename)\fP arguments and should return a unique string\&.

.PP
This option only influences imports without a layer name\&. Without this option the plugin will warn on anonymous layers\&.
.SS "Example with some options"
.PP
.nf
const postcss = require("postcss")
const atImport = require("postcss\-import")

postcss()
  \&.use(atImport({
    path: ["src/css"],
  }))
  \&.process(cssString)
  \&.then((result) => {
    const { css } = result
  })
.fi
.PP
.SH "\fRdependency\fP Message Support"
.PP
\fRpostcss-import\fP adds a message to \fRresult\&.messages\fP for each \fR@import\fP\&. Messages are in the following format:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  type: 'dependency',
  file: absoluteFilePath,
  parent: fileContainingTheImport
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
This is mainly for use by postcss runners that implement file watching\&.

.PP
